This a QTE (quick-time-events) based FMV (full motion video) game. It's poorly made (as of gameplay), but has more or less good cinematography. There's nothing really to add to it.
Would I recommend it? No, it's not worth the money.
Cons:
- bad acting;
- poor choreography;
- poor writing (as in, none whatsoever).
- counter-intuitive controls;
- boring gameplay;
Pros:
- cinematography is revelantly good.
Verdict: avoid buying it, or at least try the demo first (it's free, obviously), if trailer got your all psyched about playing an old-schoold FMV-game.
